# Merge perfect, drop the rest

distill: skill_distill/captures/2026-08-22_cursor_orchestration-outside-editor.md

**Perfect** means all of: not draft, base is `main` / `dms-v2` / `dms-integrated-engine`, `mergeable=MERGEABLE`, no conflicts, and these checks are SUCCESS: `lint-type-test`, `base-install`, `protected-paths`, `rls-proof`, `secrets-scan`. Local `pytest -q` already ran green on the same SHA.

When a PR is perfect, squash-merge it. Do not wait for a human. Cloud-agent `gh` is read-only; CI job `auto-merge` is the merge. If that job cannot merge (review required), it enables GitHub auto-merge.

Do **not** merge when any required check failed, the PR is draft, dirty/behind, or it weakens a refusal / reclassifies hostile SQL / hand-edits `contract/*.json` / adds `_C2_ALLOWLIST` names. Those are not perfect.

## Merge tiers

Approved 2026-10-06 12:02 MYT (FAST LANE, relayed by Netie Lead).

1. `tier:fast` applies to UI, docs, tests, cleanup that keeps an attic copy of what it removes, and features behind a flag that is off by default and byte-identical when off. A `tier:fast` PR merges on green required CI (the 5 push checks: `lint-type-test`, `base-install`, `protected-paths`, `rls-proof`, `secrets-scan`) plus one second-model AGREE on the exact head SHA. The AGREE comment names its model family, e.g. `AGREE (grok-4.7, different family from writer claude-opus-5-5) @ <sha>`. PR Bot's CLEAR is the CI result, not a separate serial wait. Post-merge R-0003 (Cortex Check) still runs on the merge SHA; if it returns NO, revert the merge immediately.
2. `tier:full` applies to everything else, and always to any PR touching auth or grants, keys, routing, prove pins (the proving baseline pin `279cbd85`), the contract or import-linter invariants, or scoring, eval and abstain paths. It keeps the existing bars unchanged: PR Bot CLEAR on the exact head, a different-family AGREE on the exact head as a separate comment, and post-merge R-0003 by Cortex Check, then Lead DONE/BLOCKED. A head move voids CLEAR and AGREE in both tiers.
3. PR Bot bounces any `tier:fast` PR that touches the paths in rule 2 to `tier:full`. If no label is present, the PR is `tier:full`. When unsure, full.
4. No CI check is weakened, skipped or made optional by either tier. Every existing invariant stays as-is: one writer per branch, nothing declared PASS, `DMS_L2_ENABLED=1` never committed, protected-paths rules.
5. GitHub labels `tier:fast` and `tier:full` already exist in the repo.

## Remove useless work

- Do not add LangGraph, CrewAI, n8n, Money Gainer, or Outlier scraping.
- Do not keep a dead search box, duplicate blurb, or a parked item that is only "review this capture".
- Do not open a second orchestrator. Cortex already is the loop.
- Close or skip draft PRs that duplicate a landed fix. Do not pile drive-by refactors onto a green PR.
